  "_readme": "Fixed copy of PRD-021-commercial-auto-2026.10.json. The only problem with the original was in studios.rating: 5 of its 8 factor items (the whole 'RISK FACTORS' group, plus the base premium) carried no `coverage` field. The importer (vxImportProductStudioExport in assets/js/data.js) only attaches a rating item to a coverage's premium group when that item's OWN `coverage` field names one of the entries in studios.coverage -- the group heading ('RISK FACTORS', 'BASE PREMIUM') is not read as a coverage. Those 5 items imported fine and showed up on Rating Factors, but priced nothing: the base premium is correctly unattached by design (the engine recognises it by name), but the other 4 need a real `coverage` value. This copy adds one to each ('Auto Liability' or 'Physical Damage', by which risk it actually prices), gives each a real rate table, and adds studios.formulas so every coverage rates through a formula rather than just its default chain -- both patterns already used correctly by RAT-FACTOR-001/002/003 in the original file.",

